1.4 Glycan Structure Annotation
This dataset only contains glycan composition information. However, for the advanced glycan structure analysis below, structural information is needed. A workaround is to assign these compositions with the most possible glycan structures. The glyanno package can help.

raw_exp &lt;- raw_exp |&gt;
  # Here we add a new `glycan_structure` column,
  # using the most possible structure `glyanno` assigned to each composition.
  mutate_row(
    glycan_structure = glyanno::comp_to_struc(
      glycan_composition,
      species = "Homo sapiens",
      glycan_type = "N",
      structure_level = "topological",
      return_best = TRUE
    )
  ) |&gt;
  # Some compositions cannot be assigned to any known structures in the database.
  # We regard these as false positive identifications and remove them.
  filter_row(!is.na(glycan_structure)) |&gt;
  standardize_variable()

raw_exp
#&gt; 
#&gt; ── GlycomicSE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#&gt; ℹ Abundance assay: 144 samples, 66 variables
#&gt; ℹ Glycan type: N
#&gt; ℹ Row data fields: glycan_composition &lt;comp&gt;, glycan_structure &lt;glydb_st&gt;
#&gt; ℹ Column data fields: group &lt;fct&gt;
#&gt; ℹ Metadata fields: exp_type &lt;chr&gt;, glycan_type &lt;chr&gt;, scale &lt;chr&gt;

glyanno::comp_to_struc() returns all possible matches by default. Here we set return_best to TRUE to get only the best match. This returns a glyrepr::glycan_structure() vector with the same length as the input glyrepr::glycan_composition() vector, with NA for those unmatched compositions.
Note: If you run the code yourself and this is your first time using glyanno, call glyanno::build_glyanno_cache() first to build the cache. This makes the annotation process much faster.

1.5 Data Preprocessing
Raw quantification data needs preprocessing before analysis—that’s just a fact of life in omics. Typical steps include normalization, missing value imputation, and batch effect correction. Rather than making you implement these tedious steps manually, glyclean provides a comprehensive preprocessing pipeline. Just call auto_clean() on your GlycomicSE object and you’re good to go.

clean_exp &lt;- auto_clean(raw_exp)
#&gt; 
#&gt; ── Removing variables with too many missing values ──
